SCOURGE — car-specific work notice
==================================

This repository contains car-specific changes, documentation, reference
code and scripts built on:

  SCOURGE — run your own software on Linux-based Gen5W head units
  Copyright (C) 2026 The SCOURGE Project contributors
  https://github.com/nickles-lee/hkg_SCOURGE
  Licensed under AGPL-3.0-only (see LICENSE)

The upstream project and its contributors made the head-unit tooling,
packages, runbooks and tests possible. This repository is a selective,
car-specific derivative: it is not a full copy of the upstream project and
does not redistribute firmware images, OEM binaries, OEM-derived artifacts,
raw diagnostic exports, personal data or secrets. (The upstream product
default account `car`/`electric` is a documented factory default, not a
secret; change it on your unit.)

Prior art and related research:

  IONIQ 5 (LG Gen5W) infotainment research
  https://github.com/NecktiedHummingbird/ioniq-5-Reverse-Engineering

That project's QEMU/VM and security research was used as prior art,
especially for Android Auto and micom/Bluetooth findings. Its public release
explicitly excludes raw diagnostic exports and OEM material; none of that is
included here either.

All vehicle work described here was performed on the owner's own car, parked
and off-road, with backups and rollback. Nothing here is a jailbreak guide,
a firmware update procedure, or a claim that a method works on another
vehicle.

The files in reference/qml and reference/daemon are first-party SCOURGE
code modified for this car, sanitised (owner IPs, SSIDs, BSSIDs, entity IDs
and webhooks replaced with placeholders). Files under reference/systemd are
unit-file references. No stock/OEM QML file (for example the home-screen
Advanced.qml) is redistributed; add-climate-tile.py patches your own copy.

